Time Bank Community Participation
Agreement
Last Updated: 15/9/2026
These Community Guidelines form part of the Terms of Service of Neighbour Time Bank (“Platform”). By
creating an account, selecting “I Agree,” accepting or posting a task, or otherwise participating
in the Time Bank community, you agree to comply with these rules.
Violation of these rules may result in cancellation of a task, loss of Time Credits, temporary
suspension, permanent removal from the Platform, and, where appropriate, referral to
emergency services or law-enforcement authorities.
1. Respect and Equal Treatment
All users must treat one another with dignity and respect.
Users must not engage in:
● threats, intimidation, harassment, bullying or stalking;
● discriminatory or hateful conduct;
● sexual harassment or unwanted sexual behavior;
● deliberately abusive or humiliating communication;
● exploitation of another person’s age, disability, financial circumstances or vulnerability.
Older adults must be treated as equal members of the community and must not be pressured
into accepting tasks because of their age or available free time.
2. Lawful Use Only
The Platform may only be used for lawful community activities.
Users must not use the Platform to request, arrange, facilitate or participate in:
● theft, fraud, deception or financial exploitation;
● violence or threats of violence;
● illegal transactions;
● unauthorized access to another person’s property, accounts or personal information;
● transportation, storage or transfer of unlawful items;
● any activity prohibited by applicable law.

A user who reasonably believes that a task involves unlawful conduct must stop participating
and report the task through the Platform.
3. Accurate Identity and Information
Users must provide accurate information when registering and must not impersonate another
person.
Users may not:
● create an account using another person’s identity;
● intentionally provide false verification information;
● allow another person to perform a task using their account;
● misrepresent their qualifications, abilities or experience.
The Platform may require reasonable identity verification for access to particular services.
4. Safe and Appropriate Tasks
Tasks must be appropriate for the person accepting them.
Users must not pressure another user to perform a task that the person believes is unsafe,
inappropriate or beyond their physical ability.
The Platform may restrict or remove tasks that create an unreasonable safety risk.
Health information provided through a connected wearable may be used for safety or task
recommendations only in accordance with the Platform’s Privacy Policy and the user’s consent.
A health-based recommendation does not constitute medical advice or a guarantee that a task
is safe.
5. Financial Protection
Unless specifically supported by an approved Platform function, users must not ask another
user to:
● disclose passwords, PINs or authentication codes;
● provide access to bank accounts or financial accounts;
● transfer money outside the Platform;
● sign financial or legal documents on another person’s behalf;
● lend substantial amounts of money;
● purchase unusually expensive items;
● provide credit-card or banking information.

Users should never surrender control of their financial accounts to another community member.
Suspected financial exploitation must be reported immediately.
6. Time Credits
Time Credits represent participation within the Platform’s Time Bank system and are subject to
the applicable Time Credit Rules.
Users must not:
● falsify task completion;
● artificially create tasks to generate credits;
● trade accounts;
● manipulate recorded working time;
● threaten another user in order to obtain credits.
The Platform may investigate suspicious activity and correct, freeze or remove improperly
obtained Time Credits in accordance with its Terms of Service.
7. Personal Property
Users must respect another person’s property.
A task participant may use, move or handle another person’s property only to the extent
reasonably necessary to complete the agreed task.
Taking, retaining, damaging or using another person’s property without permission is prohibited.
8. Privacy
Users must not disclose another user’s private information without permission.
This includes:
● home address;
● telephone number;
● health information;
● financial information;
● photographs or recordings;
● private messages;
● family information;
● real-time location.

Information obtained while completing a task may only be used for the purpose of completing
that task unless the user has separately consented to another use.
9. Communication
Platform communication tools should be used whenever reasonably possible so that users have
access to reporting and safety functions.
Users must not pressure others to move conversations to another communication service for the
purpose of avoiding Platform safety protections.
10. Reporting Dangerous Conduct
Users should immediately report:
● threats;
● harassment;
● fraud;
● theft;
● suspicious financial requests;
● unsafe tasks;
● missing persons;
● physical harm;
● exploitation of an older or vulnerable adult.
If there is an immediate danger, users should contact the appropriate local emergency service
before contacting Platform support.
11. Platform Enforcement
Depending on the seriousness of a violation, the Platform may:
1. issue a warning;
2. remove a task;
3. restrict certain features;
4. temporarily suspend an account;
5. permanently terminate an account;
6. preserve relevant account records as permitted or required by law;
7. cooperate with authorized public authorities where legally required or permitted.
Serious misconduct may result in immediate suspension without a prior warning.
12. User Agreement

By selecting “I Have Read and Agree”, the user confirms that:
● the user has had an opportunity to read these rules;
● the user agrees to follow them;
● the user understands that violations may result in loss of access to the Platform; and
● these Community Guidelines form part of the user’s agreement with Neighbour Time Bank.
[ ] I have read and agree to the Time Bank Community Participation Agreement.
